1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,860
Last time, we met the seven materials.

2
00:00:09,110 --> 00:00:12,850
And we asked: a rubber band, and a wooden ice-cream stick.

3
00:00:13,130 --> 00:00:15,140
Which one can bend without breaking?

4
00:00:15,651 --> 00:00:17,011
Snap it, or bend it?

5
00:00:17,061 --> 00:00:18,321
Let's test them!

6
00:00:18,371 --> 00:00:19,861
Hold on to your answer!

7
00:00:20,141 --> 00:00:21,541
We have three tests.

8
00:00:21,801 --> 00:00:23,191
Test one: pull!

9
00:00:25,862 --> 00:00:27,332
You against the Buddies!

10
00:00:27,592 --> 00:00:28,822
Lock in first.

11
00:00:29,092 --> 00:00:30,912
One finger for every point.

12
00:00:31,192 --> 00:00:33,662
A little spider is hiding in this video.

13
00:00:33,942 --> 00:00:35,142
Can you spot it?

14
00:00:35,721 --> 00:00:37,021
Today you'll learn:

15
00:00:37,225 --> 00:00:39,155
What a physical property is.

16
00:00:39,356 --> 00:00:40,806
What strength means.

17
00:00:41,005 --> 00:00:42,455
Strong or fragile.

18
00:00:43,219 --> 00:00:44,159
Are you ready?

19
00:00:44,599 --> 00:00:45,369
Three!

20
00:00:45,749 --> 00:00:46,409
Two!

21
00:00:46,779 --> 00:00:47,429
One!

22
00:00:47,849 --> 00:00:48,569
Go!

23
00:00:48,998 --> 00:00:50,628
Here is a strip of paper.

24
00:00:50,918 --> 00:00:52,028
Look closer.

25
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:53,090
Watch.

26
00:00:53,660 --> 00:00:55,360
A finger pushes the strip.

27
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:57,060
It bends.

28
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:59,050
We can observe that.

29
00:00:59,253 --> 00:01:01,063
Now one weight hangs on it.

30
00:01:01,643 --> 00:01:02,873
The strip holds.

31
00:01:03,443 --> 00:01:04,633
We count: one.

32
00:01:05,243 --> 00:01:06,603
We can measure that.

33
00:01:09,307 --> 00:01:10,527
Say it with me!

34
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:14,748
The physical property of a material is something that you can measure

35
00:01:14,768 --> 00:01:15,918
or observe.

36
00:01:20,389 --> 00:01:25,069
The physical properties you will learn are strength, flexibility, the ability to

37
00:01:25,089 --> 00:01:28,999
float or sink in water, waterproof and transparency.

38
00:01:29,062 --> 00:01:30,662
Today: the first two!

39
00:01:31,968 --> 00:01:32,848
Round one.

40
00:01:33,148 --> 00:01:35,148
Two strips, paper and fabric.

41
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:38,148
Same length, same thickness: a fair test.

42
00:01:38,418 --> 00:01:39,858
We hang weights on each.

43
00:01:40,128 --> 00:01:41,538
Which one holds more?

44
00:01:41,848 --> 00:01:42,908
One, paper.

45
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:44,338
Two, fabric.

46
00:01:44,618 --> 00:01:45,738
Three, the same.

47
00:01:46,028 --> 00:01:47,508
Show me with your fingers.

48
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:53,960
Locked in!

49
00:01:54,088 --> 00:01:54,688
Three!

50
00:01:55,068 --> 00:01:57,198
Same size, so they hold the same!

51
00:01:57,248 --> 00:01:57,858
Two!

52
00:01:58,028 --> 00:01:59,598
My school bag is fabric.

53
00:01:59,678 --> 00:02:01,148
It carries ten books!

54
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:01,990
Two.

55
00:02:02,609 --> 00:02:03,759
Look closer.

56
00:02:04,379 --> 00:02:05,349
One weight.

57
00:02:06,049 --> 00:02:06,669
Two.

58
00:02:07,289 --> 00:02:08,109
Three.

59
00:02:08,319 --> 00:02:09,569
Watch the edge.

60
00:02:10,149 --> 00:02:11,269
A tiny tear!

61
00:02:11,889 --> 00:02:13,219
It runs across.

62
00:02:13,789 --> 00:02:15,099
The paper tears.

63
00:02:15,455 --> 00:02:16,715
Now the fabric.

64
00:02:17,315 --> 00:02:18,115
Three.

65
00:02:18,715 --> 00:02:19,475
Four.

66
00:02:20,085 --> 00:02:20,905
Five.

67
00:02:21,535 --> 00:02:22,225
Six.

68
00:02:22,955 --> 00:02:23,665
Seven.

69
00:02:24,315 --> 00:02:25,055
Eight!

70
00:02:25,264 --> 00:02:26,814
The threads pull tight.

71
00:02:27,364 --> 00:02:28,884
But the fabric holds.

72
00:02:29,243 --> 00:02:32,543
More weights before it tears means a stronger material.

73
00:02:32,823 --> 00:02:34,773
Fabric is stronger than paper.

74
00:02:37,410 --> 00:02:37,740
Oh!

75
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,820
The size was the same.

76
00:02:39,930 --> 00:02:41,560
The material was not!

77
00:02:41,607 --> 00:02:42,637
Two fingers?

78
00:02:42,907 --> 00:02:44,127
One finger up!

79
00:02:44,550 --> 00:02:45,530
Be a thread!

80
00:02:45,810 --> 00:02:46,800
Shrink down.

81
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,010
Quietly.

82
00:02:50,298 --> 00:02:52,568
You are one thread in a fabric bag.

83
00:02:53,224 --> 00:02:55,834
Many threads cross over you, and under you.

84
00:02:56,490 --> 00:02:58,360
Five heavy books drop in!

85
00:02:59,778 --> 00:03:01,158
The handles lift.

86
00:03:01,928 --> 00:03:03,338
You are pulled tight.

87
00:03:03,998 --> 00:03:05,208
You do not break.

88
00:03:06,058 --> 00:03:07,238
You do not tear.

89
00:03:07,898 --> 00:03:10,058
The bag holds, all the way home.

90
00:03:12,265 --> 00:03:14,425
Pulled, without breaking or tearing.

91
00:03:14,705 --> 00:03:15,825
That is strength!

92
00:03:16,251 --> 00:03:17,401
Say it with me!

93
00:03:18,115 --> 00:03:21,285
The strength of a material is its ability to be pulled or

94
00:03:21,305 --> 00:03:23,655
pushed without breaking or tearing.

95
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:30,280
Test two: drop!

96
00:03:30,430 --> 00:03:32,530
I'll throw this glass cup on the floor!

97
00:03:32,734 --> 00:03:34,304
Something is not safe.

98
00:03:34,574 --> 00:03:36,754
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

99
00:03:37,034 --> 00:03:37,994
Hold on!

100
00:03:43,505 --> 00:03:44,635
Arms crossed?

101
00:03:44,905 --> 00:03:46,065
One finger up!

102
00:03:46,355 --> 00:03:48,205
Never break things to test them.

103
00:03:48,475 --> 00:03:50,175
Broken glass is sharp.

104
00:03:50,521 --> 00:03:51,261
Oops.

105
00:03:51,341 --> 00:03:52,401
Sorry, cup!

106
00:03:52,822 --> 00:03:55,342
An adult tests it safely, in a box.

107
00:03:55,553 --> 00:03:56,703
Look closer.

108
00:03:57,283 --> 00:03:58,813
The metal cup falls.

109
00:03:59,423 --> 00:04:00,173
Clang!

110
00:04:00,773 --> 00:04:01,953
It bounces.

111
00:04:02,461 --> 00:04:03,991
The glass cup falls.

112
00:04:04,631 --> 00:04:05,361
Crack!

113
00:04:05,951 --> 00:04:06,981
It breaks.

114
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:12,260
Glass is fragile, but metal is strong.

115
00:04:12,690 --> 00:04:15,910
A glass cup breaks easily when it is dropped, but a metal

116
00:04:15,930 --> 00:04:17,060
cup does not.

117
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:20,670
Show me your score hand!

118
00:04:20,950 --> 00:04:22,000
More than one?

119
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,660
You beat the Buddies.

120
00:04:23,940 --> 00:04:24,970
Two fingers?

121
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:26,250
High five!

122
00:04:26,903 --> 00:04:28,363
Did you spot the spider?

123
00:04:28,653 --> 00:04:31,163
It was on its thread, by the letterboxes!

124
00:04:31,433 --> 00:04:32,733
Tell someone at home.

125
00:04:33,459 --> 00:04:35,659
Let's read today's key words together!

126
00:04:35,949 --> 00:04:36,709
Ready?

127
00:04:36,996 --> 00:04:38,356
Physical property.

128
00:04:40,143 --> 00:04:41,023
Strength.

129
00:04:42,368 --> 00:04:43,198
Strong.

130
00:04:44,536 --> 00:04:45,486
Fragile.

131
00:04:46,951 --> 00:04:47,891
Well done!

132
00:04:48,888 --> 00:04:50,098
Two tests done.

133
00:04:50,378 --> 00:04:51,758
Test three: bend!

134
00:04:52,018 --> 00:04:54,488
The rubber band, or the ice-cream stick?

135
00:04:54,538 --> 00:04:55,938
Snap it, or bend it?

136
00:04:55,991 --> 00:04:57,581
Find out in Part Two!

137
00:04:58,941 --> 00:05:00,042
Say it with us!

138
00:05:00,842 --> 00:05:01,592
Ready?

139
00:05:01,715 --> 00:05:02,375
One!

140
00:05:02,715 --> 00:05:03,415
two!

141
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,895
Now you know!
